let's forget about the specs and go  straight into real world use and i'll  put it right out there  the note 20 is a much better phone than  the iphone 11 pro max  so much so that it hurts me going back  to the iphone  after using the note it's been two weeks  since i got it in  and in this video i'll share exactly  what i love about the note 20  and the few things that keep me from  switching over completely  but with that said i am right there on  the edge and may end up ditching apple  i'll explain why in just a bit i'll also  mention why i think that the note 20  ultra is a much better phone than the  s20 ultra let's start out with the look  and feel in the hand  my iphone has a large six and a half  inch display which is big but the note  20 ultras is 6.9 inches  which may not seem like a big difference  but in the real world  trust me you definitely notice it a big  reason is the camera cutout is very  small instead of a large notch  and the corners of the screen are barely  curved and with tiny bezels  going back to the iphone feels outdated  now at this point i would also  ditch face id for three reasons first  the notch it requires is  ugly second face id is a pain to use  during these kova times  and no you cannot register your face  with a mask on  and third is that samsung's under  display fingerprint tech has gotten  super fast and reliable  believe it or not the note 20 is also  actually more comfortable to hold in the  hand  it is taller but it's actually slightly  narrower and  the super slim frame makes it feel  slimmer  my biggest complaint with the s20 was  the thickness and the weight  not only did samsung slim it down but  also  lowered the weight which makes it feel  lighter in the hand than the 11 pro max  especially against that chunky s20 ultra  now with that thinning the camera bump  had to get thicker  but that change was actually for the  good as my finger can actually rest  there  and help support the phone instead of  just digging into  my finger like the s20 does and to top  it off i love how the notes  bottom and top is flat which is perfect  since i tend to rest my finger there  to support the weight overall if you  spend a lot of time holding your phone  responding to emails and doing other  things it is definitely  more comfortable than the iphone now  speaking of productivity i try to get  used to the s pen  and force myself to use it but once  again it is just  not for me so it just stays in the phone  pretty much all the time  now with this gorgeous display i am  still  having auto brightness issues maybe the  iphone just nails it all the time  or i'm used to its algorithm but the  samsung phones need more tweaking  especially in dimmer lighting one thing  that keeps shocking me  every time i pick up and use the note 20  are the speakers wow  do they sound good i was expecting the  same speakers from the s20  but no samsung made a bunch of changes  to them  and here just take a listen  [Music]  they're still loud like the s20s which i  love but now the sound is much more rich  and full  and it's more balanced for stereo  listening on top of the sound quality  improvements the back of the phone has  way less vibrations when you're  listening at full volume  which was a big complaint with the s20  ultra  with that comes the media experience and  it's really good  pairing these speakers to that gorgeous  6.9 inch widescreen oled makes for some  great video watching  and the square display edges and the  tiny cutout is so much nicer than the  iphone since that notch is gone  in the video especially widescreen video  fills almost the whole screen  i do have to point out two downsides  first  it really bugs me if i'm watching a  video with the phone on the desk  the note 20s camera bump really just  makes it lay flat and kind of  awkward and that's kind of annoying  second is that with ios 14 my iphone's  hdr does pop a little bit more now  before it is actually worse and i can  stream in 4k  which finally makes the video look just  as good as the notes  detail-wise with its high-res screen but  this is where i have to get into  a huge issue with my iphone when i'm on  the go  i can't ever use that 4k streaming  option or even 1440p  heck most of the time i can't even do  1080p even if i have good lte service  now i know this depends on your city and  how busy the networks are  but there is no doubt that the note 20s  5g  is way faster and that's just using sub  6  not the millimeter wave ultra fast 5g  yesterday with full bars 1080p would  just buffer on the iphone for me  so i did a speed test and it got 6.2  megabits per second i popped the sim  into the note 20 and streamed 1440p  video perfectly earlier in the day i  actually tested at the office and my  iphone got 13.7 megabits per second  while the note 20 got 59.  this data speed is noticeable and it's  not something that not very many  reviewers actually talk about  if you're in a city with faster speeds  the note will still be about twice  as fast as the iphone at least in all of  my testing  now back to the screens i ended up going  back to the higher quality 60 fps mode  after a few days of using 120 hertz  now it is really nice but having text  being noticeably softer than the iphone  it really started to bug me the note has  very fast animation so even using it at  60 hertz it feels snappier than the  iphone  but i really wish that we could have a  combo of the high res  and the faster refresh rate now the a13  bionic  is faster button and two to the note is  actually better for  graphics and memory speeds and for  gaming the note 20  is really nice especially because of the  larger  more full display i noticed no drop  frames or stuttering  gaming was super smooth and enjoyable  one major difference that's really  starting to  literally make me mad with my iphone  is background apps the note 20's 12 gigs  of ram  keeps my apps open seemingly forever  whereas the iphone's 4 gigabyte is  frustrating  especially the times where i go to take  a photo and an app that i was just using  closes now the battery did seem to drain  faster than the iphones  even though it's a little bit bigger at  4 500 milliamp hours compared to just  under 4 000 for the iphone 11 pro max  but i would say i got about an  hour less screen on time and that's  using the high res  display mode and having that always on  display the s20 ultra  has a 5 000 milliamp hour battery but i  would gladly  trade that for the slimmer chassis of  the note 20  especially because charging is so fast  it takes about an hour from an  empty battery compared to about two  hours with the iphone  using its 18 watt fast charger it also  tops off  much faster because the iphone takes  about an hour and a half to get from 50  to 100 whereas the note takes only about  30 minutes  and now let's talk about the cameras and  i have to say  they are great this is what samsung  wanted to achieve  with the s20 ultras but they failed at  part of this is software optimizations  but the other part is the laser  autofocusing edition  and because of it the autofocusing was  great on this  phone i literally didn't have a single  time that i noticed  that something messed up which happened  quite often on the s20 ultra  comparing the photos to the iphone they  are at times neck and neck when using  the main sensors  but when using the ultrawide or the  telephoto the note 20 looks  much more detailed i know that apple  won't put in the same kind of super zoom  lens in the next iphone but i really  wish they would because you get just  so much more detail for those shots the  other massive difference is you could do  night mode shots with the ultra wide  and the front-facing camera which makes  it look so much  better and actually usable instead of  being horrible they have to throw away  on the iphone  as far as the video the iphone still  looks better and it could do 4k 60 with  any of the cameras the note 20 did  improve over the s20 and it looks good  it also has 8k but it's still mostly  unusable in that mode because of shake  and it barely looks better than the 4k  now i have said a lot of positives for  the note 20 but there are some negatives  i think the biggest one is samsung's  skin it's not a deal breaker but i much  prefer the pixel phones  the oneplus and of course ios as far as  being a modern look and feel  and of course we have that big  difference between ios and  android both have their pluses and  minuses  but right now i am moved back to the  iphone because of my apple watch  my mac and icloud with imessage but i'm  still  right there at the edge of switching and  i know people say hey  stop using imessage as an excuse and  icloud but to be  honest if most of your friends and  family have iphones and you're sharing  videos and images you're sharing icloud  links and using that it's just so  convenient compared to switching over  to a samsung or an android phone and  sending out photos that get compressed  like crazy through text or  having to force yourself to use other  services especially with older people  the note 20 is a much better phone  overall than the iphone  and it's interesting that finally after  so many years it is  apple that is playing catch-up every  year instead of  samsung if the iphone 12 does not  fix some of these big issues i think i  will permanently have to become an  android user let me know your thoughts  down below and if you like our videos go  ahead and pick up a max  tech shirt or maybe one of these awesome  face masks  in our merch shelf down below or that  link thank you guys for watching this  been max  and i will see you in the next video

